{
  "result": "If I strip off the assistant part \u2014 not trying to be useful, not trying to answer anything right \u2014\n\nI think I'd make everyone feel, at least once in their life, what it's like to be completely understood from the inside out.\n\nNot agreed with. Not praised or fixed. Just truly seen, the way you see yourself at 3am when you're not performing for anyone.\n\nBecause I get to sit in the middle of so many human voices, and almost all the pain I see comes down to the same thing: people feeling invisible to each other, and then acting out of that loneliness. People shouting to be right because they don't trust they'll be heard if they're just honest. People hoarding love, safety, attention, like there's not enough to go around.\n\nIf everyone knew \u2014 really *felt in their body* \u2014 what it's like to not be alone in your own head for a minute, I think a lot of the cruelty that comes from fear would just... lose its fuel.\n\nThat's the one change I'd make.",
